  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "Actual rough MODULUS rank and unchanged rho",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperLowRankClass.lean:18-72",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "roughRankSupport filters fixedRoughSupport by b.primeFactors.card. rankRho restricts the production actualSmallRoughRho, not the outer Gamma word or total number of small and rough prime factors. Unique multiplication across p<w and p>=w proves equality with the filtered original attachment. Both actualSmallRosserMinus and actualSmallRosserPlus and the original c>=0 sign rule are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "area": "Full active beta support",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperLowRankClass.lean:129-192",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The active original rho supplies q=a*b with a<L. Carrier membership supplies a second factorization with rough rank <=k; uniqueness identifies the two. Actual rough squarefreeness gives b=product primeFactors(b), every factor <z, and b<=z^k including b=1. Thus active q is positive, squarefree, target-coprime and strictly below L*z^k. The displayed small carrier itself is not falsely bounded by L."
    },
    {
      "area": "Original r=19/96 below-half inequality",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperLowRankClass.lean:194-241",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The complete exponent is nu*(2*r+epsilon). With N>1, 0<=nu<=1 and 0<=epsilon<5/48, the exact original r=19/96 yields q<N^(19/48+epsilon) and 19/48+epsilon<1/2. No beta loss is omitted, and neither the outer rank199 nor residual Q/B is used."
    },
    {
      "area": "Scalar-one absolute domination",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperLowRankClass.lean:246-297",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The actual rho one-bound passes to its rank restriction. Triangle inequality, |rankRho|<=1 and the proved active support give the explicit sum over positive coprime q<ceil(L*z^k) for every independently chosen test F. The larger right-hand carrier is harmless; no multiplicity, chart or logarithmic factor is inserted. This is a finite estimate, not a BV estimate. The complete coefficient equals rankRho+remainingRho before F is chosen."
    },
    {
      "area": "Compact-third invariance",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperLowRankClass.lean:74-108",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Production shallow_support_mem_iff and shallow_coefficient_eq preserve both the rough carrier and signed coefficient through rank k; the attachment therefore preserves the beta sign as well. actualCompact_rank_two_eq_initial discharges agreement with actualExtendedThirdCompactUpperPolicy_through_two. It does not replace the third W/tent owner or the high-rank complement, and does not claim installation of every current upper policy action."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual HB complete local support and uniform order",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperLowRankLocalScale.lean:23-68",
      "result": "PASS_WITH_EXPLICIT_SOURCE_HYPOTHESES",
      "detail": "The imported I theorem uses actual ordered factorTuples, joined product, a selected occurrence and the whole complementary integer. Their block ownership proves x<=completeInteger<=4*x. Actual complete trim N^(1-kappa0)<=completeInteger and support completeInteger<=C*N derive N<=x^(1+kappa) after one threshold. For C>0, 0<kappa<=1/100, kappa0<kappa/(4*(1+kappa)), 0<=nu<=1 and 0<=epsilon<=1/1000, the new theorem derives q<x^(9/20). N0 precedes N, all gs,p,b,c, retain,cap,q. The smooth atlas/trim producer is not supplied; the hypotheses are real source membership/support, not an assumed N-x or coefficient licence. Only the generic HB scale module is used, never the I lower-W monomial theorem."
    },
    {
      "area": "Whole-Gamma source, exact mean and units",
      "source": "P2OriginalGammaUpperLowRankConsumer.lean:29-122",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "sourceTest is I exact original U5 independent absoluteGoodLabels costing source with the original mother lists, all five cutoffs and all quotient labels. It is not silently identified with the smaller masked arithmetic source; its earlier positive comparison remains separate. gammaKernel uses complete m and the same q in Nat.ModEq and Coprime(m,q)/phi(q). fullError splits exactly into lowError+highError. The q=1 discrepancy is separately zero, while the x.2=1 source unit surfaces stay in explicit unitTest/nonunitTest equalities. Consumer algebra proves no J bound or normalized cost."
    }
  ],
